# effects.vip
#
# A fixture for the effect columns. Nothing else in this repo uses one:
# before this file, the only effect anywhere was a single `fx=V42` inside a
# style, so the path from a `.vip` through the driver to the registers had
# never been exercised by a song, in either direction.
#
# One note per effect, held across the rows it acts on, because vibrato,
# portamento and arpeggio all modulate a *sounding* note. Turning the note
# off between them — the obvious way to write this — produces a file where
# the driver slides and arpeggiates silence, and nothing reaches the
# registers at all.
#
# Load:  :e projects/effects.vip

@song  bpm=150  edit_step=1  current=00

@instr 00  a=0  d=0  s=1.00  r=0  duty=0.50  vol=1.00   # a plain gate

@phrase 00
  # step   PU1
  00       C-4:00:0F:V42    # vibrato, depth 4 rate 2
  01       ===
  02       ===
  03       ===
  04       ===
  05       ===
  06       ===
  07       ===
  08       E-4:00:0F:S20    # portamento up to E-4 at 32 period units a frame
  09       ===
  0A       ===
  0B       ===
  0C       C-4:00:0F:A47    # arpeggio: root, major third, fifth
  0D       ===
  0E       ===
  0F       ===
